  "summary": "Fort Wayne City Council delayed a decision on a $120,250 renewal contract for 36 Flock Safety ALPR cameras after an initial 5-4 rejection, hearing presentations from Flock and Fort Wayne Police about how the technology works, data sharing, audits, and 180-day retention. Council members and about 20 public commenters raised privacy and transparency concerns; a final vote is scheduled for July 28.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A $120,250 contract to renew the services for 36 cameras was initially shot down by council members before they decided to delay the final decision until July 28.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Data is stored for 180 days before it's deleted",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Fort Wayne Police Department has to agree to share information with other agencies before they can access the data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's really a question of safety versus personal liberty.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
